			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838825">
									

<p>Aside from the unprofessional writing style, it doesn't make sense that knowing about the dice will get you terminated. The dice itself isn't an infohazard which warrants a termination upon discovery. Even if it needed to be hidden from level 1 below, amnestics should suffice. Also, researchers don't leave out untested variables unless if it's too dangerous/unethical. Since they were about to test if the dice will roll even with a barrier between the subject, it should've been included in the description. Other tests that should've been included was how it would react if a group were to enter its &quot;judgement zone&quot;(Please remove that. It's unnecessary and not what a researcher would normally do.) Make sure you cover all your bases.</p>
<p>Try reading <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/how-to-write-an-scp">How to Write an SCP</a> and go ask in forums to improve the style and idea of what you're writing.</p>

